index 0000000..98225c6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ANDROID-TODO.md
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+# Android port: TODO list
+
+## Touch support (currently only a basic fallback for mouse + keyboard use)
+
+Done (src/android/androidui.cpp):
+- Taps work as left clicks (Qt synthesizes mouse events from touch).
+- Long press (600 ms, finger not moving) sends a right click + context menu event.
+
+Missing, in rough priority order:
+- Scrolling lists, the project bin and the effect list by dragging (needs QScroller, but it conflicts with
+  drag & drop of clips from the bin: needs a rule such as "drag starting on a clip = DnD, elsewhere = scroll").
+- Two-finger pan and pinch-zoom on the timeline and the monitors (QML pinch/wheel handlers).
+- Selecting timeline clips by touch: a tap on a clip only moves the playhead in the tests done so far.
+- Larger touch targets for toolbar buttons, track headers, splitter handles, scrollbars and menu items.
+- Touch-friendly dragging of clip edges (trim) and of keyframes.
+- On-screen keyboard: it takes the whole screen in landscape and hides the dialog being edited.
+- Hardware keyboard shortcuts work; add a touch bar for the common ones (play, cut, undo).
+- Portrait layout (not started).
+
+## Other
+- Release signing and a real application id (still org.qtproject.example.kdenlive, debug-signed).
+- cairo-based frei0r plugins, OpenCV-based effects, Movit effects.
+- Importing very large videos uses the original file in place only when media permissions are granted.
+
+## Bugs reported from manual testing (2026-10-16), to investigate with the phone connected
+- "Rendering warning" at every project load: fixed in `previewmanager.cpp` (the missing kdenlive_render error is skipped on Android). Timeline preview rendering (needs kdenlive_render) is still unavailable.
+- Crashes (user's manual test, 5 recorded 16:50-17:24, all on the Qt main thread):
+  * 4x SIGABRT `Failed to acquire deadlock protector for QAndroidPlatformOpenGLWindow::eglSurface()` (Qt Android: `QOpenGLContext::makeCurrent` from `QRhi::create` / `QRhi::beginFrame` in the widgets backing-store flush). Qt's Android plugin gives up when the Android UI thread holds the surface lock (surface being created/resized/destroyed: new dialog/floating windows, soft keyboard showing/hiding, resume) while the Qt thread is busy. Not Kdenlive code. Ideas: find which action triggers it (repro!), avoid creating extra top-level native windows (floating docks, dialogs) while the main thread is busy, keep `windowSoftInputMode` from resizing the surface (adjustPan/adjustNothing in the manifest), try the OpenGL-less widgets backing store (QT_WIDGETS_RHI) or a newer Qt.
+  * 1x SIGSEGV (null read, fault addr 0x8) in KDDockWidgets 2.4.1: `StateDragging::handleMouseMove` -> `WindowBeingDragged::floatingWindow()` (DragController.cpp:441) while dragging a dock panel with a mouse event. Idea: on Android disable dock floating/dragging (KDDockWidgets Config flags) or guard against the null window.
+  * DOCK CRASH FIX (done): `core.cpp` drag-about-to-start hook returns false on Android (no dock dragging) + `Flag_TitleBarNoFloatButton` (mainwindow.cpp). Verified: dragging dock tabs with the mouse no longer crashes. Trade-off: panels cannot be rearranged by dragging (use layouts/presets); floating panels are gone. The 4 deadlock aborts: see 'eglSurface abort fix' below.
+  * Still needed: the user's description of what they were doing; earlier log lines had rotated out of the logcat buffer. Pull `adb logcat -b crash` / `-d | grep "Fatal signal"` right after one, symbolize with `llvm-symbolizer -e build/kdenlive-arm64/lib/libkdenlive_arm64-v8a.so`.
+- [FIX APPLIED, needs the user's retest] Editing a title clip's text with touch (title editor, `titler/`) — androidui.cpp now sets `ImhNoPredictiveText|ImhNoAutoUppercase` on every QLineEdit/QSpinBox/QTextEdit/QPlainTextEdit when focused and `MyTextItem` sets it for the scene text item; verified the keyboard gets inputType 0x80001 (NO_SUGGESTIONS). Original report: the Android keyboard opens, but changing the value deletes text irreversibly and no new text can be typed. Probably the QGraphicsTextItem input-method handling (preedit/commit, Qt::ImhNoPredictiveText missing) or the Android IME composing region. Try disabling predictive text on that widget.
+- "Pastes from clipboard on startup?": Android shows a "pasted from your clipboard" notice when an app reads the clipboard; no read at startup found in Kdenlive's code (only on paste actions). Check `adb logcat | grep -i clip` at launch to find the caller (maybe a Qt/KDE widget such as the Paste action or a line edit).
+- Not a bug, a note: toolbar icons were resized by the user, folders were added in the bin (settings/project persist OK).
+
+## Scoped-storage audit of media jobs (done, verified on the Pixel 9 Pro by mouse)
+- Speed Change and Stabilize wrote their .mlt (and .trf) next to the source clip in shared storage and failed silently: fixed, both now write to AppDataLocation (Speed Change/ and Stabilize/ folders).
+- Automatic Scene Split (ffmpeg scene filter, adds range markers), Proxy (mjpeg proxy in the app cache) and Transcode work unchanged.
+- Cut-clip and custom jobs write media next to the source and were not exercised.
+
+## eglSurface abort fix (applied, smoke-tested; user to confirm in daily use)
+Cause (Qt 6.11.2 source): any new top-level window (menu, dialog, tooltip, combo popup) is a `QAndroidPlatformOpenGLWindow`; its first paint calls `eglSurface()`, which takes the single global `AndroidDeadlockProtector` flag and `qFatal`s if it is taken. The flag is held by the Android UI thread while it blocks on the Qt thread (soft-keyboard IME calls `runOnQtThread`, accessibility `runInObjectContext`), so opening a popup while the keyboard/IME is querying the text field aborts the app.
+Fix: `build/patch_qt_android_plugin.sh` binary-patches the plugin (`CraftRoot/plugins/platforms/libplugins_platforms_qtforandroid_arm64-v8a.so`, original kept as `.orig`) so the failure branch skips the frame and returns EGL_NO_SURFACE; the window retries on its next flush. Worst case is one blank popup instead of a crash. Re-run the script after any Craft reinstall of qtbase. Cleaner long-term fix: build the plugin from source with a retry loop that pumps the input-context's queued calls. Smoke test: 40 menu/context-menu open/close cycles, no abort.
+
+## Cut-clip and custom jobs (verified by mouse on the Pixel 9 Pro, 2026-10-17)
+- Extract Zone (clip monitor right-click, CutTask): ffmpeg stream copy wrote `waterfall_cascade-7-8.mov` next to the source in Movies/ and it appeared in the bin (2:05). Works unchanged.
+- Custom job: the stock "My Custom job" has an empty Executable, so it shows "Application not found" until configured. Configured it via Media Jobs > Configure Clip Jobs with Executable = the app's `lib/arm64/libffmpeg.so` (path from `dumpsys package`, changes per install), args `-i {source} -vf hue=s=0 -t 2 {output}`, extension `mp4`: wrote `waterfall_cascade-0001.mp4` (grayscale, 2 s) and added it to the bin. Works unchanged.
+- Fixed: the stock "My Custom job" Executable is now pre-filled with `KdenliveSettings::ffmpegpath()` on Android (clipjobmanager.cpp, in both the settings dialog and `getJobParameters`) when none is saved; verified after a reinstall (shows the new per-install lib path). Arguments are still empty for the stock job.
